WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:03.836
-As the US scrambles
to withdraw from Afghanistan

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:05.805
and complete the evacuation,
the same Republicans who

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:08.141
supported Donald Trump's deal
with the Taliban to withdraw

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:10.743
are now shamelessly piling on
and trying to erase history.

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:13.546
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:16.916 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.617
In order to claim
that what's happening

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:20.653
in Afghanistan right now
came out of nowhere,

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.756
you have to willfully ignore
or erase 20 years of history

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:25.191
in which the Washington elite

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.527
repeatedly lied about
how the war was going,

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.829
which is exactly
what so many in the media,

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.531
and especially
the right-wing ghouls

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.732
who got us into this mess --

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.400
the Karl Roves
and John Boltons of the world

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.768
have been doing.

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:37.937
Donald Trump himself,
the guy who negotiated the deal

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.840
with the Taliban to release
prisoners and withdraw by May,

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.041
has been on TV claiming

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.743
he would have handled
the situation better.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.144
And for some reason,

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:48.414
he's going out of his way
to compliment the Taliban

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:50.583
on their fighting
and negotiating skills.

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.118
-Taliban, great negotiators.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.987
Tough fighters,
great negotiators.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.988 line:0%
The Taliban, good fighters.

00:00:55.988 --> 00:00:57.457 line:0%
I will tell you,
they're good fighters.

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:59.124 line:0%
We have to give them
credit for that.

00:00:59.124 --> 00:01:00.426
-No, you don't.

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:03.863
You don't have to give
the Taliban credit for anything.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.531
They're the Taliban.

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:07.900
It's especially insane
to call them good negotiators

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.637
like they're trying to talk down
a used car salesman.

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.004
"This car has a lot
of miles on it,

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:13.372
but it runs like a champ.

00:01:13.372 --> 00:01:15.875
Give it to me for free
or I'll murder your family."

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.810
"Oh, alright.
Tough, but fair, Mr. Taliban.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.712
Let me talk to my manager.
And he's dead.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.247
I'm going to get you the keys."

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.749
Does Trump think

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:25.018
if he's nice to the Taliban,
they'll hang out with him?

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.618
"Great fighters,
great negotiators

00:01:26.618 --> 00:01:28.521
and great, great golfers.

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.756
Abdul Ghani Baradar,
horrible guy,

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:33.960
but I saw him eagle a par 5
from the rough.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.095
We played in a foursome
with Brooks Koepka

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.296
and Bryson DeChambeau,

00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:38.932
and you want to talk
about warring factions.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.267
Those two do not
like each other."

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.235
I mean, thank God this idiot
wasn't the chief of police

00:01:43.235 --> 00:01:45.337
in San Francisco
during the Zodiac killings.

00:01:45.337 --> 00:01:46.906
"Bad guy. Nasty guy.

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.441
But you got to give him credit
for one thing --

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:51.377
beautiful, beautiful penmanship.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:52.778
And I love those little puzzles.

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:54.514
Reminds me of the
"New York Times" spelling bee.

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:56.349
We love the pangram,
don't we, folks?

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:59.585
Don't we love
the pangram, Trump voters?"

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:01.554
If you don't know
what the pangram is,

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.688
you don't want to know.

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:05.725
It'll destroy your life.
Just -- is an evil game.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.126
Yesterday,
I spent 11 hours on it

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.128
and then I finally got Genius,
and when I told my kids,

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:12.965
they said,
"We haven't eaten yet today."

00:02:12.965 --> 00:02:14.200
And then there was
Trump's former

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.269
White House press secretary,
Kayleigh McEnany.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.504
Oh, pangram.

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:20.540
Nope. Never mind.
I didn't use the F.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.108
Who went on Fox yesterday
and made it clear

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:25.044
she's fully inhabiting
an alternate reality.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:27.179 line:0%
-Look, when
President Trump was president,

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:29.916 line:0%
you didn't see
crisis after crisis.

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:30.916 line:0%
You just didn't see it.

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:33.319 line:0%
I shudder to think about

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.622 line:0%
what Covid would have
been like under Joe Biden.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.856
-Well, she's right
about one thing --

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.657
you didn't see
crisis after crisis

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:40.059
if you were watching Fox.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.795
More than 400,000 Americans
died from COVID under Trump.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.297
Also, he got it,

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:47.066
and his rallies and White House
parties were superspreaders.

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:49.535
Trump personally helped
spread more disease

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:52.371
to more people than
a community swimming pool

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.306
filled with water
from the East River.

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:56.242
"Alright, everybody
out of the deep end.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.510
We got another mobster.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.879
Give me the long pole thing
with the hook on it.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.514
You kids want to see
what happens

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.583
when you sing to the feds?"

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:06.118
Trump's entire presidency
was crisis after crisis.

00:03:06.118 --> 00:03:08.554
His presidency
was such a disaster,

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:10.522
when it started,
I had an audience,

00:03:10.522 --> 00:03:12.292
and now we cut to Wally
so often,

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:15.061
he's getting offers
to do Scorsese movies.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.796
-Just one thing, Marty.
I don't curse.

00:03:17.796 --> 00:03:19.332
[ Laughs ]
No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:22.201
I'm just [bleep] with you,
buddy.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:26.906
-Take the sunglasses off.

00:03:29.341 --> 00:03:31.977
To say Trump didn't cycle
through crises after crisis

00:03:31.977 --> 00:03:34.513
is to ignore that much of
his inner circle got indicted,

00:03:34.513 --> 00:03:37.116
his cabinet had, like, half
a dozen corruption scandals.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:39.618
He praised Nazis,
kidnapped migrant children,

00:03:39.618 --> 00:03:41.921
fired or tried to fire
the people investigating them,

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:44.256
got caught paying hush money
to a porn star,

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:46.726
incited a violent insurrection
to overthrow an election,

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.761
helped Saudi Arabia
cover up a murder,

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:51.030
single-handedly caused
the longest government shutdown

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.197
in American history,

00:03:52.197 --> 00:03:55.167
and told the Boy Scouts a story

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:57.904
about yachts
and New York parties.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.372
-When I was young,

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:02.141
there was a man
named William Levitt

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:04.543
and he was
a very successful man,

00:04:04.543 --> 00:04:07.012
and he went out
and bought a big yacht,

00:04:07.012 --> 00:04:09.849
and he had
a very interesting life.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.551
I won't go any more than that
because you're a Boy Scouts,

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:15.054
so I'm not going to
tell you what he did.

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:17.423
Should I tell you?
Should I tell you?

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:18.858
[ Applause ]

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:24.463
Oh, you're Boy Scouts,
but you know life.

00:04:24.463 --> 00:04:26.832
You know life.

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:29.802
-That's a thing that happened.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.904
A bunch of 12-year-olds
who wanted to learn,

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.538
I don't know, about knots,

00:04:33.538 --> 00:04:34.941
and he's up there saying,

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:36.342
"I don't know
if you give out badges

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.043
for having threeways
and blowing rails,

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:41.881
but if you did, you would have
run out in the '80s.

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.182
You're Boy Scouts. You know."

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:46.185
Look, I'm not saying

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:48.387
Joe Biden doesn't
screw up or make mistakes.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:49.555
He does.

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.523
Watching him
take questions from reporters

00:04:51.523 --> 00:04:53.659
can feel like watching
the grounds crew

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:55.528
roll out a tarp
in a hurricane.

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:58.197
Don't worry. They got it.
They got it. Oh! Oh, God!

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:59.432
Ohhh.

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:01.234
The tarp just swallowed Mr. Met.

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:02.702
Of course, based on
what's been happening

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.003
at Citi Field recently,

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.905
I think Mr. Met
would happily embrace

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:08.007
the sweet release of death.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:10.309
"We're going to get you
out of there, Mr. Met!"

00:05:10.309 --> 00:05:13.179
"Leave me to die."

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:15.148
So, Biden certainly
has made mistakes.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:18.484
It's not like the withdrawal and
evacuation have been flawless,

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:20.019
even if it's
the right thing to do.

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:22.054
Even if the chaos was inevitable

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:24.123
after 20 years
of a failed quagmire

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:27.326
the foreign policy establishment
repeatedly lied about.

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:29.795
For one thing, the US should
evacuate and grant asylum

00:05:29.795 --> 00:05:32.131
to any vulnerable Afghan
who wants to come here, period.

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:35.301
A community organizer helping
to evacuate vulnerable Afghans

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:37.169
wrote in
"The New York Times" yesterday,

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:39.138
"...we're coordinating
on different platforms

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:40.806
and languages,
often all at once.

00:05:40.806 --> 00:05:43.676
We're figuring out what
Taliban checkpoints to avoid

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:46.912
and what gate at the airport is
the most accessible, if any are.

00:05:46.912 --> 00:05:48.915
We're raising money,
millions of dollars overnight

00:05:48.915 --> 00:05:50.449
to charter planes.

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:53.051
We're endlessly compiling
spreadsheets with information

00:05:53.051 --> 00:05:55.454
about Afghans who are
under threat from the Taliban.

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:58.157
We're doing this because
the American government isn't.

00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.525
That's inexcusable."

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:00.759
Shouldn't be on volunteers

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:02.995
and human rights activists
alone to figure out

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:05.464
which gates are
most accessible in Kabul,

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:08.233
since it's not even
an easy task at LaGuardia.

00:06:08.233 --> 00:06:09.435
At LaGuardia,
there are no gates.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:10.769
You just walk onto the tarmac

00:06:10.769 --> 00:06:12.671
and hail a flight the way
you would a cab.

00:06:12.671 --> 00:06:14.440
I swear, one time I printed out
my boarding pass

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.075
for a LaGuardia flight
to Los Angeles

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:19.044
and it told me
to go to Gate 65 in Terminal Z

00:06:19.044 --> 00:06:20.179
near the haunted Cinnabon.

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:21.413
I should note,

00:06:21.413 --> 00:06:23.248
we have to get our
LaGuardia jokes in while we can,

00:06:23.248 --> 00:06:24.917
because they're doing
a major renovation

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:26.351
that it looks like
it's going to be pretty nice,

00:06:26.351 --> 00:06:29.922
which sucks, because LaGuardia
is a perfect comedy word.

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:31.623
It's the Kalamazoo of airports.

00:06:31.623 --> 00:06:33.693
And yesterday's pangram.

00:06:39.231 --> 00:06:41.634
I'm starting to think the crew
is not doing the spelling bee.

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:45.538
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:47.973
-Nonetheless, getting out
is the right thing to do,

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:49.075
and Americans support it.

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:50.509
In fact, Americans
have wanted us

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:52.144
to get out of this war
for a long time.

00:06:52.144 --> 00:06:54.680
Polls have shown
that as many as 73% of Americans

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.582
want it to end, 73%.

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:58.016
Part of the problem is,
for years,

00:06:58.016 --> 00:07:00.186
the media has all
but ignored Afghanistan.

00:07:00.186 --> 00:07:02.488
But you know who wasn't
ignoring the war?

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:03.655
Defense contractors.

00:07:03.655 --> 00:07:06.659
The Costs of War Project
at Brown University

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:09.495
estimates that since invading
Afghanistan in 2001,

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:13.366
the United States has spent
$2.313 trillion on the war.

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:15.934
And "The Intercept" calculated
that $10,000

00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:18.871
invested in defense stocks
when the Afghanistan war began

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:21.406
is now worth almost $100,000,

00:07:21.406 --> 00:07:23.609
because defense stocks
outperformed the stock market

00:07:23.609 --> 00:07:26.211
overall by 58% percent
during the Afghanistan War.

00:07:26.211 --> 00:07:28.247
Now, you don't have to know
much about the stock market

00:07:28.247 --> 00:07:31.550
to know the defense contractors
profit from war,

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.452
which is why the Washington
elite are freaking out --

00:07:33.452 --> 00:07:35.688
the same reason
your weed dealer freaked out

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:36.956
when they legalized it.

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:39.625
"What am I supposed to do?
Get a job? Sell coke?

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:41.527
Oh, that's it. I'll sell coke."

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:43.996
Also, I should clarify,

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:46.065
I have no idea
how the stock market works.

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:48.000
All I know is my broker
calls me once a day

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.601
and tells me how
my portfolio's looking.

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:50.736
[ Cellphone rings ]

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:52.404
Oh, that's him now. Hold on.

00:07:52.404 --> 00:07:53.806
Hey, how's it looking?

00:07:53.806 --> 00:07:55.975
[ Gasps ]
You invested in the Mets? When?

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:58.144
Three weeks ago?

00:07:58.144 --> 00:07:59.511
What money did you use?

00:07:59.511 --> 00:08:00.813
You sold our LaGuardia stock?

00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:02.682
That's about to go sky high!

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:08.287
So the media has ignored
Afghanistan for years

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:10.122
and elite Washington
has lied to us about it,

00:08:10.122 --> 00:08:11.356
as documented by

00:08:11.356 --> 00:08:13.425
"The Washington Post's"
blockbuster reporting

00:08:13.425 --> 00:08:15.194
on what we're known
is the Afghanistan Papers,

00:08:15.194 --> 00:08:16.628
in which government officials

00:08:16.628 --> 00:08:20.165
secretly admitted "we clearly
failed in Afghanistan"

00:08:20.165 --> 00:08:21.567
and "we didn't know
what we were doing."

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:25.337
The US occupation of Afghanistan
began 20 years ago,

00:08:25.337 --> 00:08:27.806
and for basically
that entire period,

00:08:27.806 --> 00:08:29.575
our government has shielded us

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:30.909
from the reality
of what was happening.

00:08:30.909 --> 00:08:32.644 line:0%
George W. Bush
and Donald Rumsfeld

00:08:32.644 --> 00:08:34.814 line:0%
even went so far
as to make grandiose predictions

00:08:34.814 --> 00:08:36.649 line:0%
about how the war
would be viewed by history,

00:08:36.649 --> 00:08:40.319 line:0%
despite what they really knew
was happening behind the scenes.

00:08:40.319 --> 00:08:44.356
-The history of military
conflict in Afghanistan,

00:08:44.356 --> 00:08:47.960
it's been one
of initial success

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:51.763
followed by long years
of floundering

00:08:51.763 --> 00:08:55.034
and ultimate failure.

00:08:55.034 --> 00:08:56.736
We're not going to
repeat that mistake.

00:08:56.736 --> 00:09:00.406 line:0%
-What has taken place in the
last four years in Afghanistan

00:09:00.406 --> 00:09:03.942 line:0%
is an historic achievement.

00:09:03.942 --> 00:09:05.677 line:0%
And the people
who've been involved in it

00:09:05.677 --> 00:09:07.880 line:0%
can be enormously proud,

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:11.950 line:0%
and history will look back on it

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:14.486 line:0%
as having been
an amazing accomplishment,

00:09:14.486 --> 00:09:16.289
-I'm honestly not sure
if these guys were

00:09:16.289 --> 00:09:17.856
ever right about anything, ever.

00:09:17.856 --> 00:09:21.026
Like, these guys were so wrong
about so many things.

00:09:21.026 --> 00:09:22.828
There's a good chance
Don Rumsfeld

00:09:22.828 --> 00:09:23.829
wasn't even his real name.

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:25.030
It sounds like an alias

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:27.966
Dick Whitman would use
to get a job at Raytheon.

00:09:27.966 --> 00:09:30.803
Suffice to say,
history will not look back on it

00:09:30.803 --> 00:09:32.137
as an amazing accomplishment.

00:09:32.137 --> 00:09:33.872
If anything, I think
it's much more likely that

00:09:33.872 --> 00:09:36.442
when they get to the chapter
on Afghanistan in future,

00:09:36.442 --> 00:09:38.544
textbooks will just say
"file not found."

00:09:38.544 --> 00:09:41.413
Of course, in the future, there
probably won't be textbooks.

00:09:41.413 --> 00:09:44.250
You'll just get all your history
downloaded in a chip

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.217
that you put in your brain.

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:46.318
Okay, activate the chip.

00:09:46.318 --> 00:09:47.386
[ Laughs ]

00:09:47.386 --> 00:09:49.722
He said what to the Boy Scouts?

00:09:49.722 --> 00:09:52.157
Hey, it's one thing to be wrong.

00:09:52.157 --> 00:09:54.593 line:0%
I make mistakes all the time,
as anyone who watches

00:09:54.593 --> 00:09:57.463 line:0%
our Emmy-nominated corrections
segment will tell you --

